<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating the exact area of a rectangular rug with surd dimensions in the form k*sqrt(m)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A rectangular rug has length \({@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}}\text{ m}\) and width \({@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}}\text{ m}\).</p>
<p>Find the exact area of the rug, giving your answer in the form \(k\sqrt{m}\), where \(m\) has no perfect-square factors. <i>(Note: For example, write <code>18*sqrt(143)</code> to represent \(18\sqrt{143}\).)</i></p>
<p>Area = [[input:ans1]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Step 1: Recall the formula for the area of a rectangle</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = {@a@}\sqrt{{@n@}} \times {@b@}\sqrt{{@m@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Multiply the numbers outside the square roots</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@a@} \times {@b@} = {@ab@}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 3: Multiply the numbers inside the square roots using \(\sqrt{x} \times \sqrt{y} = \sqrt{x \times y}\)</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \sqrt{{@n@}} \times \sqrt{{@m@}} = \sqrt{{@n@} \times {@m@}} = \sqrt{{@nm@}}\)</p>

<p><b>Step 4: Combine the results</b></p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Area} = {@ab@} \times \sqrt{{@nm@}} = {@ta1@}\text{ m}^2\)</p>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Area} = {@ta1@}\text{ m}^2 }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
